From: Androlinzberg host integration
Subject: [PATCH] HWUI: process texture updates before hosted frame traversal

The host Ganesh pipeline owns real DeferredLayerUpdaters. Apply pending updates
before prepareTree, including frames that subsequently skip drawing. Leaving
the Layoutlib guard in place clears the pending list without updating the layer;
TextureView readback can acquire correct pixels while its cached onscreen layer
stays black. Flush uploaded/deleted textures on skipped frames as Android does.

--- a/libs/hwui/renderthread/DrawFrameTask.cpp
+++ b/libs/hwui/renderthread/DrawFrameTask.cpp
@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@
     if (CC_LIKELY(canDrawThisFrame)) {
         context->draw(solelyTextureViewUpdates);
     } else {
-#ifdef __ANDROID__
+#if defined(__ANDROID__) || defined(ARTZIG_HOST_GRAPHICS)
         // Do a flush in case syncFrameState performed any texture uploads. Since we skipped
         // the draw() call, those uploads (or deletes) will end up sitting in the queue.
         // Do them now
@@ -178,7 +178,7 @@
     bool canDraw = mContext->makeCurrent();
     mContext->unpinImages();
 
-#ifdef __ANDROID__
+#if defined(__ANDROID__) || defined(ARTZIG_HOST_GRAPHICS)
     for (size_t i = 0; i < mLayers.size(); i++) {
         if (mLayers[i]) {
             mLayers[i]->apply();
